A||N||7||CRAGAR||code 42, redhot exh manifolds???||||1||
Z||000000||CRAGAR||12-09-1999||09:52 AM||||I just set a code 42, on the drive into work this morning, engine would not pull well at all, drove 8 miles and the exhaust manifolds are red hot.  I have not cat. convertor and the exhaust system is welded.  What's the best way to troubleshoot this one?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dan||12-09-1999||10:12 AM|||| The 42 is an electronic spark control.The cherry red exhaust is also a classic symptom of a vacuum leak.Check all vacuum lines first and another thing to check is distributor timing.If those check out the go to the electronic spark control.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Richard Parnell||12-09-1999||01:51 PM||||Be sure and check your wire to the oxygen sensor.  If the o sensor is disconnected or bad I've seen the exhaust turn cherry red.||||reg||12
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||12-09-1999||02:32 PM||||Be sure to check your oxygen sensor connection.  If the o sensor is disconnected or bad it will cause the timing problem and the manifold will heat up to a nice cherry red glow.  The car will also feel like it has no power.||||reg||12
Z||000004||CRAGAR||12-09-1999||05:03 PM||||Just a quick update, I drove the car at lunch, and everything was back to normal.  No check engine light, engine would rev up to redline, and no cherry red exhaust manifolds!!!  Now what?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||12-10-1999||09:44 PM||||The mysterious self-repairing vacuum line?  Sure wish I had those, you lucky sob..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000006||dogtired||12-11-1999||01:06 AM||||The only time I ever had chreey red manifolds was because my timming was off, just a little. So with that in mind and your smptoms, I would chek my distributor and see if the hold down bolt is loose? It could be turning back and forth just enough to couse it?<BR>Just a thought? GOOD Luck!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000007||penetrator||12-13-1999||01:14 AM||||Where are the Oxygen Line connected ?<P>Maybe that can cause my stalling ? <BR>I have fierostores Headers on my engine, and i cant se if they going red because they are very thick.<P>Thanks<BR>Magnus||||reg||1
